# filesidle.ps2 - ⛔ THE NEGATIVE CONTROL for the file manager.
#
# The same ROM, the same card, the same `desk` - started with a directory
# on its command line, so the window is ALREADY UP on /SD0/DATA and there
# is something to leave alone - and a mouse that walks over the list, over
# both scroll arrows, over the menu bar and over the disk icon, and NEVER
# PRESSES A BUTTON.
#
# ⛔ Without this, every claim in run-v3files.sh is satisfied by a program
# that enters a directory on a timer, scrolls by itself, or treats a hover
# as a click.  What it has to show: the list held exactly ONE picture, no
# DESK-SEL, no DESK-OPEN, no DESK-DIR after the first, nothing launched -
# and the list it held is still /SD0/DATA's real contents, so a blank
# screen is not what passed it.
#
# ⚠ THE POINTER IS IN THE PICTURE, and unlike deskidle.ps2 this control
# cannot dodge it by walking somewhere else: hovering the list IS the
# gesture under test.  checkfiles.py counts the list's pictures only on
# frames where the sprite's 16 x 16 is clear of the list rectangle and the
# pointer has been still for SETTLE seconds, so the walk is asserted at the
# rests outside the window and the sprite's own pixels are never counted.
origin 320 240

at 2.000    move to 580 300
+1.200      move to 200 191     # row 0 of the list
+1.200      move to 200 209     # row 1
+1.200      move to 200 300     # further down it
+1.200      move to 580 300     # off, and still
+1.200      move to 504 190     # the scroll bar's UP arrow
+1.200      move to 504 390     # ... and its DOWN arrow
+1.200      move to 580 300
+1.200      move to 200 8       # the Go title in the menu bar
+1.200      move to 108 50      # the disk icon
+1.200      move to 580 300
